  "scope": "Two independent author roots reproduce the complete component and runtime CPAN archives. Author sources are removed before offline installation; unchanged callers replay after moving each installed consumer tree on all four pinned ABIs in both delivery modes, for sixteen executions per selection. The standalone result-only API projects primitive payloads through scalars, copied containers, records, variants and aliases without any input constructor selections. This selection ran at producer revision e15acb534151d359b05b68364ab35e6ab6c77073 under a recorded host-load admission ceiling of 12. Primitive-base nominal Perl acceptance covers the tested acyclic records, variants, aliases, mixed Fin guards and constructor-free results over Unit, Bool, UInt8, UInt16, UInt32, UInt64, Int8, Int16, Int32, Int64, Nat, Int, Float32, Float, String, ByteArray, Char, USize and ISize. Both author routes and full/result-only APIs reproduce complete CPAN component and runtime archives from two authors. Perl 5.36.3 and 5.38.2, each threaded and unthreaded, install them offline after author removal as prebuilt-only and build-xs deliveries and replay after physical relocation on Linux x64/glibc 2.36 with an explicit 2.36 package floor. The four accepted selections ran serially under two frozen producer revisions and recorded per-run host-load admission ceilings of 6, 8, 8 and 12; the hosted default stays 6 and the disk and memory floors never changed. Original archives, receipts, control runs, preserved non-accepted launches and selected sources at both revisions are retained; external toolchain binaries are not. The Perl caller's check counts equal the Python caller's as a consistency check, not as borrowed evidence. Other hosts need their own primitive-base nominal acceptance. Refined callbacks, owned, recursive, dependent and broader generic Subtypes remain separate work. Constructor/source entry counts and memory are unmeasured. These local runs do not establish hosted release-floor acceptance; archived absolute paths describe the original machine and are not CI prerequisites.",
